gins":0.0,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":0.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":-0.24652033406116963,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":false,"_score_shrhldr_yield":0.0,"_gate_share_shrink":0.28671455747070773,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":0.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.08270232674111888,"_gp_sbc_dilution":false,"_score_sbc_dilution":0.0,"_gate_insider_own":0.0057300003,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":3.8,"_gate_insider_buying":0.0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"CytomX Therapeutics, Inc. operates as an oncology-focused biopharmaceutical company that focuses on developing potent biologics designed to treat tumor microenvironment. The company utilizes conditional activation platform technology for oncology biologics research and development comprising the validation of targets for antibody-drug conjugates (ADCs), opening therapeutic window for novel T-cell engagers (TCEs) targeting solid tumors, and increasing the therapeutic index for immune modulators, such as cytokines; and PROBODY platform in preclinical research in areas outside of oncology. It also develops CX-904, a T-cell engaging bispecific antibody targeting the epidermal growth factor receptor (EGFR) on tumor cells and the CD3 receptor on T cells; CX-2051, a conditionally activated ADC for optimizing the therapeutic index for EpCAM-expressing epithelial cancers, including colorectal cancer; and CX-801, an interferon alpha-2b PROBODY cytokine. In addition, the company's development pipeline comprises CX-2029, a conditional activated ADC targeting CD71; and BMS-986288, a PROBODY version of non-fucosylated ipilimumab. It has strategic collaborations with Amgen, Astellas, Bristol Myers Squibb, Regeneron, and Moderna; and clinical trial collaboration and supply agreement with Merck for the evaluation of CX-801 in combination with anti-PD-1 therapy, KEYTRUDA (pembrolizumab). The company was founded in 2008 and is based in South San Francisco, California.","ceo_bio":"Dr. Sean A. McCarthy DPHIL | Chairman & CEO | Age 58 | Compensation: $1.4M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 69 people. Revenue per employee of $1.1M ranks in the top quartile among Healthcare peers, with revenue growing 26%/yr across its filed history. Stock-based compensation of $91K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 1\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (6/10).","financial_summary":["CytomX Therapeutics, Inc. is a small-cap healthcare business with a $445M market cap on $76M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +13% over the past three years and +26% annually across the full decade, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","The company is burning through $76M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","Accruals are elevated at +38.4% of assets, and Sloan showed firms building earnings through accruals rather than cash systematically underperform.","On the balance sheet, thin -35.3\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Net dilution runs at 24.7% annually, transferring value from owners to stock-based comp, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Accruals elevated at +38.4% of assets \u2014 Sloan showed firms building earnings through accruals rather than cash systematically underperform","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Piotroski score 1/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (-0.7) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Very elevated short interest (23.5% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting against the business","sev":"red","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"News sentiment sharply negative (-0.28) across 12 recent articles \u2014 the narrative has turned","sev":"red","cat":"news"},{"text":"Operating margins 29% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Financial quality metrics lag Healthcare peers","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Patent cliffs, drug-pricing reform, and reimbursement pressure \u2014 a single regulatory change can reset the pricing power that justifies the multiple.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"GLP-1 disruption across sub-sectors \u2014 weight-loss drugs are reshaping demand for orthopaedics, cardiovascular devices, and sleep-apnea treatments in ways not yet priced in.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","Valued at a 107% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk","Healthcare sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 13% over 3 months","Healthcare ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term average","Strong 6-month sector performance (30.7% return)"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"CytomX Therapeutics (CTMX) & Its Peers Critical Contrast","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/11/cytomx-therapeutics-ctmx-its-peers-critical-contrast.html","date":"2026-11-11","timestamp":1794392972.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.815,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"CytomX anticipates Varseta-M registrational study in 1H 2027 while projecting cash runway into 2H 2028 (NASDAQ:CTMX)","source":"seekingalpha